{"qid":"Q1364632","names":["Wu"],"title":"Wu","endonym":null,"capsule":"The ancient State of Wu was a polity in the lower Yangtze region during the Spring and Autumn period, famed under kings Helu and Fuchai for its military strength and rivalry with Chu and Yue. It briefly achieved hegemony in the late 6th-early 5th century BC. It was conquered and annexed by the State of Yue in 473 BC.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. This polity has not yet received individual source review: treat extents as indicative atlas convention.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Wu (state)","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Early kings of Wu (Taibo line)","nativeName":"吳國先君（太伯世系）","roman":"Wú xiānjūn","start":-750,"end":-586,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"King Shoumeng of Wu","nativeName":"吳王壽夢","roman":"Wú Wáng Shòumèng","start":-585,"end":-561,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"King Zhufan of Wu","nativeName":"吳王諸樊","roman":"Wú Wáng Zhūfán","start":-560,"end":-548,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"King Yuji of Wu","nativeName":"吳王餘祭","roman":"Wú Wáng Yújì","start":-547,"end":-544,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"King Yumei (Yimei) of Wu","nativeName":"吳王餘眛","roman":"Wú Wáng Yúmèi","start":-543,"end":-527,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"King Liao of Wu","nativeName":"吳王僚","roman":"Wú Wáng Liáo","start":-526,"end":-515,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"King Helü of Wu","nat